    "description": "Open redirect: is_local_path() only rejects a literal '//' prefix and backslashes, then trusts urlsplit(), which silently strips tab/CR/LF before parsing. A `next` value like '/\\t//attacker.example' (tab is legal in an HTTP Location header) passes the prefix check and is parsed by urlsplit as the bare path '///attacker.example', while browsers strip the control character and treat it as a scheme-relative URL, sending the victim to https://attacker.example after login or logout (the same gap also smuggles raw CR/LF into the Location value)."
